From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 02:42:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: check the ACPI _PR3 package properly

nv_acpi_power_resource_method_present() joined each pair of checks with &&, so
it only rejected _PR3 when both failed. A non-package with a count field of 1 and
a non-reference element both passed, and the first element of an empty package
was read past the end of the object.

Require a non-empty package whose elements are all references to power
resources, which is what the ACPI spec defines and what the kernel's own
power resource parsing expects. A package with more than one resource keeps
working, although the old comment asked for exactly one, since ACPI allows it
and it was accepted until now.

This decides whether RTD3 is available, so firmware that passed by accident now
loses it.

Booted on a laptop whose _PR3 is valid: RTD3 stays enabled. The rejected cases
haven't been run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia/nv-acpi.c | 34 +++++++++++++++++++++-------------
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-acpi.c b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-acpi.c
index 83d61515..1a7913ae 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-acpi.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-acpi.c
@@ -1363,6 +1363,7 @@ NvBool nv_acpi_power_resource_method_present(
     struct acpi_buffer buf = { ACPI_ALLOCATE_BUFFER, NULL };
     union acpi_object *object_package, *object_reference;
     acpi_status status;
+    u32 i;
 
     if (!handle)
         return NV_FALSE;
@@ -1383,29 +1384,36 @@ NvBool nv_acpi_power_resource_method_present(
 
     object_package = buf.pointer;
 
-    /*
-     * _PR3 object should be of type package and
-     * it should contain only one reference
-     */
-    if ((object_package->type != ACPI_TYPE_PACKAGE) &&
-        (object_package->package.count != 0x1))
+    /* _PR3 object should be of type package */
+    if (object_package->type != ACPI_TYPE_PACKAGE)
     {
         nv_printf(NV_DBG_ERRORS,"NVRM: _PR3 object is not a type 'package'\n");
         kfree(buf.pointer);
         return NV_FALSE;
     }
 
-    object_reference = object_package->package.elements;
-
-    /* Check for the reference and the actual type of the reference. */
-    if ((object_reference->reference.actual_type != ACPI_TYPE_POWER) &&
-        (object_reference->type !=  ACPI_TYPE_LOCAL_REFERENCE))
+    /* An empty package lists no power resources */
+    if (object_package->package.count == 0)
     {
-        nv_printf(NV_DBG_ERRORS,
-                     "NVRM: _PR3 object does not contain POWER Reference\n");
+        nv_printf(NV_DBG_INFO, "NVRM: _PR3 object is empty\n");
         kfree(buf.pointer);
         return NV_FALSE;
     }
+
+    /* Check for the reference and the actual type of the reference. */
+    for (i = 0; i < object_package->package.count; i++)
+    {
+        object_reference = &object_package->package.elements[i];
+
+        if ((object_reference->type != ACPI_TYPE_LOCAL_REFERENCE) ||
+            (object_reference->reference.actual_type != ACPI_TYPE_POWER))
+        {
+            nv_printf(NV_DBG_ERRORS,
+                         "NVRM: _PR3 object does not contain POWER Reference\n");
+            kfree(buf.pointer);
+            return NV_FALSE;
+        }
+    }
     kfree(buf.pointer);
     return NV_TRUE;
 }
